title: a2.1 Mindful Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Eight stakeholders. Four walk: the resident with dementia (ST-01), the care worker (ST-02), a fellow resident as walking partner (ST-04), a volunteer (ST-07). One runs the resting and listening side: the activity coordinator (ST-08). Three influence the walk without walking: family (ST-03), management (ST-05), medical and therapy staff (ST-06). Shared: the resident's health and calm. Divided on: freedom of movement versus safety, and how much of the resident's life story the System may store.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03 to SA-07.
|Type|Direct - walks, rests, listens
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - physical and mental health; calm
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - whether, where, how long; what to hear
* HV-04 Safety (high) - no falls, no getting lost
* HV-08 Identity (high) - own past, interests, tastes
* HV-07 Social connectedness (medium) - company on the walk
* HV-02 Dignity (medium) - accompanied without being guarded; addressed as an adult
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - whereabouts, life story, listening habits
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Escorted by ST-02 or ST-07, sometimes by ST-03. Walks with ST-04. Relaxes and listens with ST-08. Lives under ST-05's exit rules. Mobility and fall risk assessed by ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01, SA-03 to SA-07; holds → HV-01 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-01 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Care worker [ST-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-04, SA-06.
|Type|Direct - escorts walks, calms residents, handles incidents
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - every resident back, unharmed
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - daily exercise; calm evenings
* HV-06 Attentive care (high) - time for each resident despite other care tasks
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - lets residents choose, within time and safety limits
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - for residents, and against surveillance of own work
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Escorts ST-01; pairs ST-01 with ST-04. Works with ST-08. Employed by ST-05. Informs ST-03 of incidents. Follows ST-06's advice on exercise, falls and medication.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-02, SA-06; supports → SA-01, SA-03, SA-04, SA-07; holds → HV-01, HV-03 to HV-06; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-03, PS-05; elaborated-as → HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Family member [ST-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Family member
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-06, SA-07.
|Type|Indirect - walks with the resident at times; keeper of the life story
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - fears falls and the resident leaving the home
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - physical and mental health of their relative
* HV-08 Identity (high) - their relative remains the person they knew
* HV-02 Dignity (high)
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium)
* HV-03 Privacy (low) - may want more on whereabouts and mood than the resident would share
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Relative of ST-01. Occasional walking companion. Gives life story and listening preferences to ST-08. In contact with ST-02; may consent on ST-01's behalf.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-06, SA-07; holds → HV-01 to HV-05, HV-08.

= Stakeholder - Walking partner [ST-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Walking partner
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-04.
|Type|Direct - fellow resident, walks with ST-01
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-07 Social connectedness (high) - company on the walk
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - own physical and mental health
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - free to decline or end a joint walk
* HV-08 Identity (medium) - a shared past to talk about
* HV-02 Dignity (medium) - walks as a partner, without a helper's duties
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - shares the walk; keeps personal information private
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Fellow resident of ST-01, often with dementia too. Matched by ST-02. Has own family (ST-03) and care plan (ST-06).

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-04; holds → HV-01 to HV-03, HV-05, HV-07, HV-08; appears-in → PS-02; elaborated-as → HP-04 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Care home management [ST-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Care home management
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-02.
|Type|Indirect - sets exit policy and staffing; decides on adoption; data controller
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - liable when residents leave unnoticed or fall
* HV-06 Attentive care (high) - staffing and workload
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - quality of care
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - open versus locked doors
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - data protection for residents and staff
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-02 and ST-08; screens and insures ST-07. Responsible for the building, garden and exits used by ST-01 and ST-04.

== Graph edges ==

governs → SA-01 (exits, outdoor access), SA-02 (staffing); holds → HV-01, HV-03 to HV-06.

= Stakeholder - Medical and therapy staff [ST-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-06
|Name|Medical and therapy staff: GP or elderly-care physician, nurse, physiotherapist, psychologist
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03, SA-05, SA-06.
|Type|Indirect - assesses mobility; sets exercise programme; advises on relaxation; prescribes PRN medication
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - mobility, mood, sleep
* HV-04 Safety (high) - fall risk
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium)
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Assesses ST-01 and ST-04. Advises ST-02 on exercise and evenings, ST-08 on relaxation.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-03 (exercise), SA-05 (relaxation), SA-06 (PRN); holds → HV-01, HV-03 to HV-05; appears-in → PS-03, PS-05.

= Stakeholder - Volunteer [ST-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-07
|Name|Volunteer
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-04.
|Type|Direct - unpaid, walks with residents one-to-one
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-07 Social connectedness (high) - personal bond with the resident
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - resident enjoys the walk
* HV-04 Safety (high) - unsure how to handle disorientation, falls or exit-seeking
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - own schedule, free to stop volunteering
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - for residents; no access to medical information
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Walks with ST-01, or with ST-01 and ST-04 together. Coordinated by ST-08. Screened and insured by ST-05. Relies on ST-02 for advice from ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-04; holds → HV-01, HV-03 to HV-05, HV-07; appears-in → PS-02.

= Stakeholder - Activity coordinator [ST-08] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-08
|Name|Activity coordinator
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-02, SA-05, SA-07.
|Type|Direct - leads relaxation sessions; keeps life stories and playlists; plans walks
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - meaningful, pleasant days
* HV-08 Identity (high) - activities that fit the person
* HV-07 Social connectedness (high) - group activities, matched pairs
* HV-06 Attentive care (medium) - time per resident
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - life-story data in their care
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Works alongside ST-02. Collects life story and preferences from ST-03. Advised by ST-06. Coordinates ST-07. Employed by ST-05.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-02, SA-05; supports → SA-07; holds → HV-03, HV-05 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-04, PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-03 (§2.2).
